  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure builds in at the surface today with a light\nnorthwest flow ushering in a drier, more comfortable airmass\nover time. However, a deep trough remains carved out aloft, \ncentered over New York and proximity to this low, left over \ninstability and some light upslope flow will allow for isolated \nto scattered showers and maybe a thunderstorm to develop over \nour northeast counties with quite a bit of diurnal cu and maybe\na sprinkle or two to the west.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure fully builds over the region Thursday and Friday\nwith temperatures near to slightly below normal along with \ncomfortable dewpoints.\n\nUnsettled weather returns for the weekend, however, as a trough\ndigs into the Ohio Valley. Confidence is pretty high that \nshowers and thunderstorms will increase in coverage by Saturday \nnight into Sunday. Beyond Sunday, models diverge a bit on \nwhether the low will cut off to our west or remain transient. \nNBM maintains chance PoPs both Monday and Tuesday and that seems\nreasonable with the uncertainty.",
